# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Fixture working copies. The clone script fetches these at pinned SHAs; they
# are inputs to the agent, never part of the project. See rule 7 and the FAQ:
# "Can I use code I already have? Not as the project itself."
/fixtures/

# What `proofs/mcp_stub.py` writes if its tool is ever actually invoked. The
# proof asserts this does NOT exist, so a copy of it must never be committed --
# a stale one would make a failing run look like a passing one.
pr-calls.log

# Where the proofs write their evidence by default. The recorded runs under
# `proofs/recorded/` are committed deliberately; a fresh run's output is not.
/sandbox.json
/deny.json

# The generated site. Built from `pages/runs.toml` on demand; never committed,
# because a stale copy of a generated page is worse than no copy.
pages/_site/

# The screen recording the submission video was cut from. The video is published
# at youtu.be/Eb-URyCtBPY; a copy of the source file in the history would be
# carried by every clone of this repository forever.
*.mp4
